jobDescription:
The Professional Development and Standards (PDS) Division in ECDA develops Early Childhood (EC) and Early Intervention (EI) professionals and supports preschools to deliver holistic and inclusive care and education through setting quality standards and fostering a culture of continuous learning and innovation.

The Professional Standards and Training (PST) Branch within PDS drives the strategic thrust on developing early childhood professionals effectively. The scope of the PST Branch encompasses:
•	Setting standards for EC professional qualification programmes and work with training providers to ensure quality of programmes;
•	Certifying EC educators to ensure that they meet the relevant professional requirements to work in the sector;
•	Working with training partners to support developing skills and competencies of EC and EI  professionals through CPD courses;
•	Supporting leadership development for the EC sector

jobRequirements:
Requirements
a. Educational background in social sciences preferably with related experience; 
b. At least 1 year of experience working in the social service industry; 
c. Comfortable in spoken and written English as the position requires regular preparation and presentation of reports; 
d. Good interpersonal and communication skills; 
e. Good analytical skills and the ability to influence effectively; 
f. A team player who can work independently; and 
g. Self-motivated and resourceful

agencyDescription:
The Ministry of Finance (MOF) is responsible for managing Singapore’s fiscal policies and the structure of its economy. We work to maintain international standards and best practices in areas such as company law, accounting standards, and corporate governance principles. We aim to advance the well-being and development of Singapore by:

•	achieving a balanced budget through prudent and sustainable fiscal policies;
•	ensuring the prudent investment of the government's reserves and other public funds;
•	setting out policies for government procurement, customs regulation, accounting standards and business regulation;
•	fostering a regulatory environment conducive to business and enterprise; and
•	ensuring that businesses operating within Singapore's jurisdiction are compatible with international standards and practices, in areas such as company law, accounting standards and corporate governance principles.

jobResponsibilities:
Your main responsibilities will be to provide administrative support in ensuring efficient management of daily tasks and scheduling of engagements for your principal. The key responsibilities include:  

a. Scheduling of meetings/events/engagements.  
b. Managing calendars, emails and phone calls;  
c. Making official work trip arrangements;  
d. Administrative support for the principal, and for the Division as assigned; 
e. Assist in organising events and/or related support work for the department 
f. Maintaining records and filing systems;  
g. Taking minutes of meetings; 
h. Managing budgets and expenditure; and 
i. Any other duties assigned by your principal.

You will develop and implement strategies, policies, and projects to empower Singapore’s social service sector to have a greater positive impact. For example, you will:

• Govern and administer funding to the social service sector;
• Develop a strategy and implementation plan on how to incentivise and support greater impact measurement and evaluation in the social service sector;
• Develop a strategy and implementation plan on how to incentivise and support more intentional and outcome-oriented technology adoption within the social service sector;
• Evaluate the latest philanthropic giving and social impact investing models and trends, and develop ways for the social service sector to better leverage such systems; and/or
• Develop and maintain strategic partnerships with other social service stakeholders to develop the social service sector.

