The National Research Foundation (NRF) was set up on 1 January 2006 as a department under the Prime Minister's Office. It was set up to perform the following:

a) To provide secretariat support to the Research, Innovation and Enterprise Council (RIEC), chaired by the Senior Minister;

b) To coordinate the research of different agencies within the larger national framework in order to provide a coherent strategic overview and direction;

c) To develop policies and plans to implement the five strategic thrusts for the national R&D agenda; and

d) To implement national research, innovation and enterprise strategies approved by the RIEC, and to allocate funding to programmes that meet NRF's strategic objectives.

jobResponsibilities:
The key role of the Innovation & Research Translation (IRT) directorate is to build a vibrant Innovation & Enterprise (I&E) ecosystem that enables deep tech innovations from our universities and A*STAR to be translated into globally competitive products, services and businesses. You will lead a team that will advance the following objectives:

•	Identify emerging deep tech areas with potential for large economic growth in the future, through a deep understanding of our local peaks of excellence, global developments, and market opportunities;

•	Validate the thesis on the economic potential for these areas through: (1) a data-centric approach, (2) qualitative understanding of the R&D and innovation landscape, and (3) engagements with Key Opinion Leaders and industry experts;

•	Work with Economic Agencies to develop sector-specific strategies and tools to grow a critical mass of companies in the emerging deep tech areas;

•	Work with deep tech ecosystem partners and multipliers, such as Venture Builders, Incubators, Tech Transfer Offices etc to provide a comprehensive suite of support that enables innovation in the emerging deep tech areas;

•	Monitor the overall I&E ecosystem to identify gaps in deep tech commercialisation, particularly at the early stages of research translation; and

•	Manage relevant funding schemes that are administered by NRF in support of our efforts to grow the deep tech and I&E ecosystem.

jobRequirements:
•	Background in science, engineering, economics or public policy;

•	At least 5 years of relevant working experience preferably working on tech policy or driving innovation in a technology startup or company;

•	Strong analytical abilities with a broad sense of perspective;

•	Excellent written and verbal communication skills;

•	Ability to forge strong relationships and networks with ecosystem partners; and

•	Ability to collaborate well with others

•	[Administration Management] Proven relevant experience as a Personal Assistant, or in a similar role supporting senior management;
•	[Secretariat Support] Able to work independently with good organisational and time-management skills to provide support in secretarial matters relating to assigned principal;
•	[Stakeholder Management] Work with relevant stakeholders at various levels to obtain relevant inputs and ensure smooth coordination and transition between meetings and appointments;
•	[Adaptability] Professional and resilient, able to perform under pressure, manage short timelines and adapt to fast-paced environment with shifting priorities quickly.

jobResponsibilities:
Climate action is a priority for MSE, and is driven by the Energy & Climate Policy Division (ECPD).  ECPD is MSE’s coordinating policy desk for issues overseen by the Inter-Ministerial Committee on Climate Change (IMCCC). ECPD drives policies relating to climate science, climate adaptation and climate mitigation, including issues such as carbon pricing, decarbonising Singapore’s economy, coastal protection, and reducing urban heat. You will join the Climate Mitigation team to help Singapore navigate an uneven and complex climate landscape, domestically and internationally.

As part of the Climate Mitigation team within ECPD, you will work with a diverse range of stakeholders from the public sector (e.g. NCCS, MTI and various statutory boards), private sector and civil society on a whole-of-nation effort to mitigate climate change. Amongst many other issues, you will be: 

•	Developing strategies to realise carbon abatement through adoption of a variety of low-carbon solutions,from scaling up international carbon markets to promoting energy efficiency nationally;
•	Reviewing the price of carbon; 
•	Managing and driving the implementation of mitigation measures (such as carbon capture, utilisation and storage) within the MSE family, in collaboration with other government agencies and private sector partners; 
•	Reviewing and strengthening NEA’s capabilities to support low-carbon strategies, e.g. those in relation to NEA’s role as the carbon tax administrator and the national carbon accounting authority;
•	Developing thought leadership for international climate mitigation issues (e.g. scaling up innovative financing models to facilitate the low-carbon transition) in partnership with IMCCC agencies; and
•	Supporting inter-agency efforts in driving the triple transition of carbon, energy and economy.

As a TIER officer in the Trade Strategy and Security Division, you will be part of a dynamic team working on fast-moving pieces to help Singapore navigate changes in our geo-economic environment. You will have the opportunity to hone your strategic thinking skillset, policy acumen, and international orientation perspectives in both the economic and security domains, by:

•	Assessing the impact and implications of geo-political developments on Singapore’s economic and security interests;

•	Developing strategies, policies, options and responses to expand Singapore’s economic heft or relevance as well as strengthen Singapore’s economic resilience;

•	Preparing and executing communications and engagement strategies with key public and private sector stakeholders;

•	Organising and representing MTI at various high-level inter-agency platforms related to economic, security, and geo-political portfolios; and

•	Collaborating and networking with various internal and external stakeholders.

jobRequirements:
We are looking for dedicated team players who thrive in a fast-paced environment with:

•	Relevant field of study in International Relations, Political Science, Public Policy, Economics, Business, Finance, Accounting or any related discipline;

•	Keen interest in the geo-political environment, as well as economic and security issues;

•	Experience in policy formulation and data analysis;

•	Excellent analytical, writing, communication, and presentation skills; and

•	Strong project management and stakeholder management skills.

jobDescription:
The Trade and International Economic Relations (TIER) cluster drives the formulation of Singapore's foreign economic policy and advances Singapore's economic interests in the international economic arena.

MTI’s International Trade Division (ITD) is charged with protecting and advancing Singapore’s economic interests by:

* Supporting free trade and open markets;
* Upholding and strengthening the rules-based multilateral trading system as embodied in the World Trade Organisation (WTO);
* Deepening economic integration with like-minded countries through free trade agreements (FTA) and bilateral investment treaties (BIT);
* Driving initiatives in regional economic fora such as the Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation (APEC); and
* Advancing our companies’ interests abroad rigorously, including by lowering barriers for Singapore exports

jobResponsibilities:
Responsibilities

As an ITD officer, you will be assigned to one of four specialised teams covering trade in goods, digital economy and services, investment, or multilateral trade policy. You will deepen your knowledge, skills and expertise on a myriad of international trade issues and apply them in the following areas:

* Developing and implementing Singapore’s foreign economic policy;
* Representing Singapore in bilateral/multilateral trade and investment negotiations;
* Participating in international meetings and conferences;
* Providing advice to the Singapore Government on trade policy matters;
* Collaborating with external stakeholders, such as Singapore-based companies, business chambers and the general public;
* Ensuring Singapore’s full and timely implementation of international trade obligations; and
* Analysing international developments and their potential implications on Singapore

jobRequirements:
Requirements

* Trained in Economics, Law, Political Science, International Relations, Accounting, Business or related disciplines is preferred, but not essential
* Keen interest in international economic affairs and negotiation;
* Strong analytical and conceptual abilities, with an eye for detail;
* Excellent written and oral communication skills;
* Ability to work well in teams and in a fast-paced and dynamic environment; and
* Willingness to travel frequently

• Keen interest in international economic affairs and negotiations;
• Strong analytical and conceptual abilities, with an eye for detail;
• Excellent written and oral communication skills;
• Self-starter, versatile and adaptable to different environments;
• Ability to work well in teams and engage people;
• Ability to work in a fast-paced and dynamic environment; and 
• Willingness to travel frequently

jobResponsibilities:
You will be involved in the following:

•	Work closely with Singapore and International Judges as well as Judicial Officers in matters affecting cases before the SICC and on appeals from the SICC;
•	Manage cases filed in or transferred from the GDHC to the SICC through analysing, reviewing, monitoring and processing documents in accordance with the applicable legislation, rules, practice directions, standard operating procedures and policies;
•	Draft case summaries, papers, notices and general correspondence and liaise with lawyers, self-represented persons and other stakeholders (including external agencies) to facilitate smooth proceedings and the efficient disposal of cases;
•	Compile, verify and maintain accurate case information and statistics, preparing reports including providing analysis of the statistics where appropriate, and recommend measures to enhance the operations of the SICC;
•	Establish, review and streamline existing operational processes to improve quality of work and productivity to meet the key performance indicators of the SICC;
•	Manage and provide support in the development and implementation of operational systems or changes thereto or in administering the operations of the SICC;
•	Conduct legal research and analysis with a view to making recommendations on issues affecting the operations of the SICC; 
•	Review and enhance rules of court, practice directions and practices, and make recommendations to address operational or system implications; and  
•	Assist in the functions and work of the Registry in general (including working with other divisions in the Supreme Court) and as assigned.

TIER officers in the US Division are part of a dynamic and dedicated team responsible for advancing Singapore’s economic engagement with key markets and regional organisations in North America and Latin America, including the United States. You will work on creative and innovative initiatives with colleagues in MTI and our economic agencies that will develop your international economic perspectives, capabilities and experience by:

• Analysing and reporting on geostrategic developments and trends that affect the flows of goods, services, and investments;

• Formulating and refining strategies, policies and plans that enhance Singapore’s bilateral and plurilateral economic relations with the Americas, often in consultation and coordination with other ministries and agencies across the Whole-of-Government;

• Networking and developing connections with foreign government and business counterparts;

• Preparing and executing communications, consultations and engagements with key stakeholders in the business community and general public;

• Organising and representing MTI in visits, meetings, negotiations and conferences.

jobRequirements:
Requirements

•	A tertiary qualification in any discipline; a background in Business, Supply Chain Management, Information Technology, or Cybersecurity is an advantage.
•	Preferably with at least 3 years of experience in Procurement, Contract Management or a related field;
•	Good interpersonal and communication skills, with the ability to engage and advise stakeholders at various levels;
•	A proactive, self-motivated disposition with the ability to work in a fast-paced and dynamic environment;
•	The ability to work independently as well as collaboratively as a team player.
•	A positive mindset and willingness to go beyond the scope of procurement work to support the agency’s broader mission.
If you share our passion to make a difference in the cyber security landscape, take up the challenge and apply now.
All applicants will be notified of whether they are shortlisted or not within four weeks of the closing date of this job posting. 
For any issues with the application, you may drop your resume with us at csa_recruit@csa.gov.sg

