jobResponsibilities:
Your role includes the following:

• Identify opportunities and risks in the Digital and Information domains;
• Set strategic priorities and goals for MDDI family;
• Ensure coherence in the formulation and operationalisation of strategies across the organisation through internal and external engagement platforms;
• Align the resource allocation in MDDI family with MDDI’s strategic priorities; and
• Strengthen governance to ensure the achievement of strategic objectives.

jobRequirements:
•	At least 5 to 10 years of working experience in a government agency, international organisation, or technology organisation, with a keen interest in international issues/challenges that impact on the digital economy, digital security and digital society and the implications on Singapore;
•	Trained in Economics, Law, Political Science, International Relations, International Political Economy, Business or related disciplines is preferred, but not essential;
•	Ability to sense-make domestic priorities and international developments, assess and translate them into strategic roadmap(s) to pursue Singapore’s international digital (diplomacy) objectives (International policy development);
•	Ability to balance and coordinate top-down strategy alignment and bottom-up agency inputs. (International policy formulation, alignment and coordination);
•	Ability to build and sustain partnerships and institutional linkages with bilateral and multilateral stakeholders. (International stakeholder engagement);
•	Excellent writing and presentation skills;
•	Strong analytical, conceptual and organisational skills;
•	Excellent inter-personal communication skills and stake-holder management skills;
•	General awareness of and interest in current affairs, economics and technology developments;
•	Ability to work in a fast-paced and dynamic environment; and
•	Willingness to travel.

Please note that only shortlisted candidates would be notified.

For more information on careers in MDDI, please access the link (https://www.mddi.gov.sg/join-us/careers/life-at-mddi/). For more information on our job vacancies, please access Careers@Gov (https://www.careers.gov.sg/) and search for “MDDI” in the Search bar.

agencyDescription:
The National Research Foundation (NRF) was set up on 1 January 2006 as a department under the Prime Minister's Office. It was set up to perform the following:

a) To provide secretariat support to the Research, Innovation and Enterprise Council (RIEC), chaired by the Senior Minister;

b) To coordinate the research of different agencies within the larger national framework in order to provide a coherent strategic overview and direction;

c) To develop policies and plans to implement the five strategic thrusts for the national R&D agenda; and

d) To implement national research, innovation and enterprise strategies approved by the RIEC, and to allocate funding to programmes that meet NRF's strategic objectives.

jobRequirements:
•	Background in Mass Communication, New Media, Design & Media preferred;
•	Minimum 2 years of relevant working experience in communications, media relations, public affairs, content development or a related field;
•	Excellent communication and interpersonal skills with the ability to work effectively with internal teams, external partners and senior stakeholders;
•	Meticulous and a strong team player who is self-motivated and comfortable working across different types of projects;
•	Keen interest in science and technology topics; 
•	Experience in science communication would be useful, though not mandatory.

jobResponsibilities:
We are looking for a proactive and dynamic individual to join the Financial Governance Team (FGT). In this role, you will help to strengthen MSF’s financial governance, including grant governance, through policy development, compliance, data & analytics, and cross-agency coordination. 

To be a strong contributor, you will need to:
•	Understand governance and risk management concepts and requirements; 
•	Apply concepts to develop governance policies;
•	Partner MSF’s divisions in the management of grants in compliance with the Instruction Manual on Grants Governance and continuously improve policies, processes and systems to strengthen grant governance and enhance operational efficiency; 
•	Monitor and report on governance and compliance standards, including identifying trends and areas for improvement; and
•	Leverage on data, analytics and AI tools to raise governance standards.

The scope of governance and risk management will primarily relate to financial control and grant administration, and will extend to performance evaluation and cross-agency coordination.

Responsibilities:

You will be part of a team responsible for improving financial and grant governance standards in MSF through policies, capability building and data analytics. 

To do so, you will need to partner with MSF divisions and Company Limited by Guarantee (CLG)  entities to:
•	Review and develop governance frameworks, processes, and systems to meet specific targets and timelines; 
•	Validate MSF divisions’ compliance with governance standards; 
•	Utilize and deploy AI tools for better understanding of, and compliance with, governance requirements; 
•	Develop and raise financial governance competencies among MSF’s grant officers; and
•	Drive and support data analytics framework and processes to meet risk management, fraud detection, investigation, and other reporting requirements.

You will also be required to oversee and collaborate with MSF divisions to implement programme evaluation plans to improve accountability and ensure that programme objectives are achieved.

