Reporting to the Assistant Director, your role is to lead a team of case workers responsible in the triage of enquiries received by PSV to determine the level of intervention and right siting of these enquiries and undertake crisis case management duties such as immediate safety planning and intervention work for high-risk child abuse, domestic violence and vulnerable adults experiencing violence, abuse or neglect. You will be working closely with PSV’s professional partners to ensure an effective protection system for children and young person, domestic violence and vulnerable adult survivors.

Responsibilities:
As a Senior Manager, you will:
• Supervise a team of Intake and Response case workers:
✓ undertaking triage and consultation of enquiries to determine the level of intervention and right sitting of these enquiries such as if it meets the threshold for statutory intervention or it can remain in the community for intervention;
✓ undertaking crisis management to high-risk cases on-site that involve child abuse, domestic violence and vulnerable adults, conduct safety assessment and implement immediate safety planning to ensure their safety, during and after-office hours;
• Oversee strategic planning of Intake and Response operational polices, workflows and protocols with regular reviews to improve effectiveness and efficiency of the team’s functions;
• Identify and engage key professionals to collaborate and build up interface to facilitate a smooth service delivery;
• Lead implementation and review of new initiatives to support for Intake and Response operational needs; and
• Oversee staff development to ensure professional capacity of the team by identifying training needs.
